//     encoded instead of ≈ 38 B as text. Client-chosen `document_id` and the envelope ids (namespace_id, tenant_id,
//     event_id, operation_id) stay strings. Id fields carry the suffix `_bytes` (decision N80);
//   * an event carries at most 256 ids in total across all its lists. A larger set is paged as consecutive events of
//     the same type written in the SAME transaction, with `page` (0-based) and `page_count` plus the group key named on
//     each message. A consumer treats a group as complete only when every page has been seen;
//   * above 4,096 ids (16 pages) the event is sent ONCE with `ids_elided = true`, empty id lists and the counts.
//     Consumers then read the ids from the store by `document_id`;
//   * a delete is an O(1) marker event (`DocumentDeleted`): no id list at all (decision N115). The async index consumer
//     deletes by the indexed `(namespace_id, document_id)` query, and the expunge's row purge waits until every
//     registered consumer cursor has passed the tombstone's `event_seq`, the `seq` of this very event (decisions N119,
//     N139);
//   * every encoded event is ≤ 16 KiB by construction; the CHECK `octet_length(payload) <= 16384` on the outbox is only
//     the backstop.
